1
00:00:02,794 --> 00:00:04,378
اَعُوْذُ بِاللهِ مِنَّ الشِّيْطَانِ الرَّجِيْمِ۝

2
00:00:04,500 --> 00:00:05,918
بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمَانِ الرَّحِيْمَ۝

3
00:00:07,015 --> 00:00:12,402
اَلْحَمْدُ لله  وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِنَا محمد وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًا كَثِيْرا

4
00:00:13,789 --> 00:00:20,167
We talked about the Islam, of Sydina(سيدنا) Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه.

5
00:00:20,554 --> 00:00:22,046
We talked about his Daw'ah(دعوة).

6
00:00:22,457 --> 00:00:25,148
We talked about the trials, he went through.

7
00:00:25,661 --> 00:00:35,213
Now, Rasool Allah ﷺ has given the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم permission to leave Makkah.

8
00:00:36,358 --> 00:00:41,681
Whoever wants to leave and go to Al-Habasha(الحبشه), Abyssinia, you're free to go.

9
00:00:42,853 --> 00:00:49,374
Because the persecution was reaching to a limit where it was becoming very difficult to handle.

10
00:00:50,130 --> 00:00:53,667
And with all of the Sabr(صبر) of the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم and their patience,

11
00:00:53,984 --> 00:00:57,540
but Rasool Allah ﷺ wanted to make a way out for them.

12
00:00:57,564 --> 00:01:03,125
So he gave them permission to go to Abyssinia, and many did.

13
00:01:05,824 --> 00:01:11,496
Among the ones, who stayed behind was Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه who wanted to remain with his beloved,

14
00:01:12,569 --> 00:01:19,264
but then he decided that he also has to leave for Abyssinia.

15
00:01:21,641 --> 00:01:29,749
So he travels, out of Makkah and he reaches a few days, distance away from Makkah.

16
00:01:32,411 --> 00:01:34,656
And he reaches a place called Barq-Ul-Ghamaad(برق الغماد),

17
00:01:35,707 --> 00:01:42,375
where he meets with Ibn Dughanna(ابن دغنه), who was the leader of Al-Qara(القاره), a tribe called Al-Qara(القاره).

18
00:01:42,921 --> 00:01:46,563
Ibn Dughanna(ابن دغنه) told Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه, Where are you heading.?

19
00:01:48,119 --> 00:01:50,456
Abu Bakr As-Siddique(ابوبكرالصديق) said:

20
00:01:51,081 --> 00:01:57,630
أخرجني قومي فَأريدو أن أخرُجَ في الأرض أسيحو فيها وَأعبُدالله

21
00:01:58,612 --> 00:02:03,705
He said: My people have driven me out of my land.

22
00:02:04,342 --> 00:02:07,572
So, I want to travel and worship Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ.

23
00:02:09,573 --> 00:02:12,102
I'm going to travel in the earth, the earth belongs to Allah

24
00:02:12,427 --> 00:02:13,423
ألأرض لله

25
00:02:14,115 --> 00:02:15,712
And I'm going to worship Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ.

26
00:02:18,090 --> 00:02:23,043
Ibn Dughanna(ابن دغنه) responded by saying and keep in mind this is a man who's not from Makkah.

27
00:02:25,655 --> 00:02:29,444
But he knows Abu Bakr(ابوبكر), he heard about Abu Bakr(ابوبكر), he said:

28
00:02:30,667 --> 00:02:35,618
يا أبابكر إنَّا مِثلك لا يَخرجُ ولا يُخرج،

29
00:02:36,975 --> 00:02:40,732
 فَإنَّك تَكسب المعدوم، وتصل الرحم

30
00:02:41,405 --> 00:02:48,403
وتقرض ضعيف، وتعينو على نوائل بالحق ، فاَنَ جعارلَّك

31
00:02:49,994 --> 00:02:58,909
He said: A man like you of your status, it's not appropriate for him to leave his land,

32
00:02:59,328 --> 00:03:02,140
nor is it appropriate for him, to be driven out.

33
00:03:03,027 --> 00:03:09,503
Because you are a man, who assists the needy and is kind towards his kinship

34
00:03:10,202 --> 00:03:12,195
and you are generous towards the guest.

35
00:03:12,770 --> 00:03:16,983
And you support the poor, and you stand up for every good cause.

36
00:03:17,747 --> 00:03:21,529
Therefore go back and I will give you my protection.

37
00:03:23,892 --> 00:03:26,322
There was a system in Arabia called Al-Ijarah(ألإجاره)

38
00:03:27,350 --> 00:03:29,986
where you provide protection for somebody.

39
00:03:31,280 --> 00:03:36,915
The rules of this system is that if I have a status in my people and I'm a leader of a clan

40
00:03:37,225 --> 00:03:39,730
I can give protection for someone.

41
00:03:40,547 --> 00:03:47,879
Now, the rule is: Is that I do not allow that to be violated even if it's going to cost me my life.

42
00:03:48,628 --> 00:03:51,353
Therefore, the people used to honor the Ijarah(اجارة)

43
00:03:51,521 --> 00:03:57,697
because they know that there's gonna be blood that is spilled, if there's a violation of the protection.

44
00:03:58,587 --> 00:04:05,436
So, Ibn Dughanna(ابن دغنه) taking that position shows you, how much respect he had to Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) when he was Mushrik(مشرك),

45
00:04:05,658 --> 00:04:08,118
I mean Ibn Dughanna(ابن دغنه) was a Mushrik(مشرك), he wasn't a Muslim

46
00:04:08,753 --> 00:04:13,683
but the reputation of Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) was so high and everybody knew about it.

47
00:04:13,919 --> 00:04:17,825
That Ibn Dughanna(ابن دغنه) was willing to give Ijarah(إجارة) to Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه.

48
00:04:17,849 --> 00:04:23,511
Now keep in mind that usually people from outside Quraish(قُرَيْشْ)

49
00:04:23,538 --> 00:04:26,498
would not give Ijarah(اجارة) to somebody from Quraish(قُرَيْشْ)

50
00:04:26,928 --> 00:04:29,631
because Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) are seen as the highest.

51
00:04:30,393 --> 00:04:36,674
Therefore, they didn't see it appropriate for them to give Ijarah(اجارة) for somebody from Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

52
00:04:37,600 --> 00:04:41,277
But Ibn Dughanna(ابن دغنه) was willing to risk that

53
00:04:41,500 --> 00:04:44,582
and he went ahead and took Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) into Makkah and said:

54
00:04:44,781 --> 00:04:47,023
I am giving him my protection.

55
00:04:48,726 --> 00:04:51,327
Now the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ), they came to Ibn Dughanna(ابن دغنه) and they said:

56
00:04:51,761 --> 00:04:54,440
We're not gonna violate your protection, however

57
00:04:56,030 --> 00:05:00,074
we want you to make a condition on Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) that he prays at home.

58
00:05:01,493 --> 00:05:04,137
We do not want him to pray publicly outside of his home.

59
00:05:05,571 --> 00:05:09,650
Because if he does that, then he will deceive our women and our children.

60
00:05:10,568 --> 00:05:13,641
So make him pray at home, we will honor your protection.

61
00:05:15,966 --> 00:05:18,453
Ibn Dughanna(ابن دغنه) went to Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) and said: This is the agreement.

62
00:05:18,587 --> 00:05:20,362
Do you accept Abu Bakr(ابوبكر).? He said: Yes I accept!

63
00:05:21,810 --> 00:05:25,794
So now Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه would only pray at home.

64
00:05:28,212 --> 00:05:33,919
After some time passed, you know this was against the habit of Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه,

65
00:05:34,085 --> 00:05:40,077
I mean, he's the one who asked for the proclamation of the message, in the first place.

66
00:05:40,122 --> 00:05:42,305
He's the one who went to Rasool Allah ﷺ and said:

67
00:05:42,441 --> 00:05:43,044
نَستَعْلَنْ

68
00:05:43,124 --> 00:05:46,670
We want to publicly proclaim Islam.

69
00:05:47,244 --> 00:05:53,270
So, for him, praying at home was not something that he was used to,

70
00:05:53,325 --> 00:05:55,652
he used to always do it in public in front of everyone.

71
00:05:56,822 --> 00:06:02,177
So he decided that in order not to break the agreement that he made with Ibn Dughanna(ابن دغنه).

72
00:06:02,532 --> 00:06:06,428
He should pray in the front yard of his house.

73
00:06:07,440 --> 00:06:10,947
So He's still within the house, but it's public.

74
00:06:12,084 --> 00:06:16,307
So now, Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه would be praying in his front yard

75
00:06:18,943 --> 00:06:22,886
and Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) was described as having a very soft heart

76
00:06:22,911 --> 00:06:27,062
whenever he would recite the Ayat(آية) of Qur'an he would cry, tears would roll down his cheek.

77
00:06:28,315 --> 00:06:35,678
And that's why, when Rasool Allah ﷺ told, he said that Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) should lead the people in Salah(صلاة).

78
00:06:36,366 --> 00:06:43,120
Ayesha رضي الله عنها, she said that my father has a very soft heart and if he prays, he would cry.

79
00:06:43,557 --> 00:06:44,797
 So have Umar(عمر) pray.

80
00:06:45,699 --> 00:06:49,525
So that was the Salah(صلاة) of Abu Bakr As-Siddique(ابوبكرالصديق), he would come to tears, very fast.

81
00:06:51,591 --> 00:06:54,592
So Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه would be praying in his front yard

82
00:06:54,611 --> 00:07:01,032
and all of the children and women and youth would come and gather and just watch Abu Bakr As-Siddique(ابوبكرالصديق) praying.

83
00:07:01,318 --> 00:07:02,723
 It was a very impressive scene.

84
00:07:04,154 --> 00:07:08,106
So the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) got angry because they know the power of Salah(صلاة).

85
00:07:08,986 --> 00:07:14,211
They know that Salah(صلاة), if the people see it, if they see somebody praying true Salah(صلاة) with Khushoo(خشوع),

86
00:07:14,982 --> 00:07:16,632
that this would attract them to Islam.

87
00:07:17,230 --> 00:07:19,617
So they went to Ibn Dughanna(ابن دغنه) and they said:

88
00:07:19,785 --> 00:07:22,643
Our agreement with you was that he doesn't pray publicly.

89
00:07:23,968 --> 00:07:26,760
So, Ibn Dughanna(ابن دغنه) goes to Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه and says:

90
00:07:26,784 --> 00:07:30,666
Listen the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) are not gonna allow you to do this

91
00:07:30,690 --> 00:07:33,513
so you either go back and pray in your room,

92
00:07:33,822 --> 00:07:36,340
otherwise you hand me over my protection.

93
00:07:36,578 --> 00:07:38,535
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه said:

94
00:07:38,773 --> 00:07:42,236
I'm handing you over my protection and I'm happy with the protection of Allah.

95
00:07:43,951 --> 00:07:45,458
أرضى بِجَوارالله

96
00:07:45,962 --> 00:07:48,781
I'm happy with the protection of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ.

97
00:07:51,496 --> 00:07:55,643
You remember yesterday when you talked about the test of Allah to Az-Zunairah(الزنيره),

98
00:07:55,946 --> 00:07:59,444
when Allah took away her sight to test her Eeman(ايمان).

99
00:07:59,565 --> 00:08:05,176
Well the same thing happened to Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) as soon as the Ijarah(اجارة) was ended, the protection was ended

100
00:08:05,580 --> 00:08:08,058
 and he went to pray in front of Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه) publicly.

101
00:08:08,445 --> 00:08:15,239
One of Sufaha Al-Quraish(سفها القريش), one of the ignorant among Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) came and hit Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه.

102
00:08:16,008 --> 00:08:18,829
So Abu Bakr As-Siddique(ابوبكرالصديق) was speaking to Al-Waleed Bin Mugheera(الوليدبن مغيره), he's saying:

103
00:08:18,997 --> 00:08:21,292
Can't you see what this ignorant man is doing?

104
00:08:21,843 --> 00:08:24,329
Al-Mugheera(المغيره) said: You are the one, who brought it on yourself.

105
00:08:24,855 --> 00:08:26,552
Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) would only say,

106
00:08:26,814 --> 00:08:29,767
ربي إنك حليم ، ربي ما أحلمك، ربي ما أحلمك

107
00:08:29,791 --> 00:08:32,092
O Allah, You're so compassionate and merciful.

108
00:08:32,790 --> 00:08:34,650
He was beaten up, but he would say,

109
00:08:34,675 --> 00:08:37,360
O Allah, you are very compassionate and merciful, Al-Hamdolillah(الحمدلله).

110
00:08:38,466 --> 00:08:40,037
You know, we praise Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ for everything.

111
00:08:40,775 --> 00:08:42,969
If something good happens, we say Al-Hamdolillah(الحمدلله).

112
00:08:43,669 --> 00:08:47,068
If something bad happens we say, Al-Hamdolillah(الحمدلله) it's all from Allah.

113
00:08:48,440 --> 00:08:51,518
We are property of Allah, He has the right to do with us whatever He wants.

114
00:08:52,866 --> 00:08:59,109
We talked about the knowledge of Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه, to what it's called Fiqh Al-Waqiah(فقه الواقع), the current affairs.

115
00:08:59,149 --> 00:09:03,851
He knew about the different tribes, qualities.

116
00:09:05,340 --> 00:09:12,576
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ took him along with him, to introduce himself to the tribes in Hajj(حج).

117
00:09:13,397 --> 00:09:16,132
Because that's when all of the tribes gather.

118
00:09:16,878 --> 00:09:20,023
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ would go around to the different tribes

119
00:09:20,644 --> 00:09:27,159
offering Islam to them, and asking them for protection, An-Nusra(النصره).

120
00:09:28,303 --> 00:09:30,436
And Rasool Allah ﷺ did that for a very long time.

121
00:09:30,461 --> 00:09:34,877
Rasool Allah ﷺ was looking for An-Nusra(النصره), protection for the religion.

122
00:09:36,029 --> 00:09:39,070
So he would take along with him, Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه.

123
00:09:39,094 --> 00:09:43,582
Now this story that I'm going to mention was narrated by Ali Bin Abi Talib رضي الله عنه.

124
00:09:44,653 --> 00:09:49,434
Ali Bin Abi Talib(علي بن ابي طالب) said: We were visiting the different tribes in their camps.

125
00:09:51,250 --> 00:09:55,190
So, we came to this tribe Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه was a spokesman.

126
00:09:56,600 --> 00:09:59,598
He went and he asked them, where are you from.?

127
00:10:01,138 --> 00:10:03,139
They said: From Rabiyah(ربيعة)

128
00:10:04,240 --> 00:10:06,189
He said: From which part of Rabiyah(ربيعه).?

129
00:10:07,018 --> 00:10:07,492
They said;

130
00:10:07,516 --> 00:10:09,165
من هامته العظمى

131
00:10:09,537 --> 00:10:11,384
He said: Which part of Haam Ma Tal Uzma(هامته العظمى).?

132
00:10:11,725 --> 00:10:13,401
They said: From Dahal Al-Akbar(دهل الاكبر).

133
00:10:14,765 --> 00:10:23,924
Now, Rabiyah(ربيعة) is a tribe in Iraq, and the sub tribe is Haam Ma Tal Uzma(هامته العظمى),

134
00:10:24,646 --> 00:10:26,327
which means the great forehead.

135
00:10:26,932 --> 00:10:29,786
And then Dahal Al-Akbar(دهل الاكبر) means, Dahal(دهل) the Great.

136
00:10:30,451 --> 00:10:33,688
So there's Dahal(دهل) the great, and there's Dahal(دهل) the small.

137
00:10:34,165 --> 00:10:40,485
And it's a very fine line between these tribes because they all fall under Rabiyah(ربيعة).

138
00:10:40,792 --> 00:10:43,157
So they said Dahal Al-Akbar(دهل الاكبر) from the great Dahal(دهل)

139
00:10:43,721 --> 00:10:46,660
which is kind of a proud name, the great Dahal(دهل).

140
00:10:48,195 --> 00:10:49,885
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه said;

141
00:10:49,925 --> 00:10:56,880
Well than is Auf(عوف) the man, whose said, there's no free man in his Valley does he belong to you?

142
00:10:57,829 --> 00:10:58,649
They said: No

143
00:10:59,406 --> 00:11:02,164
He said: What about Al-Haufazaan(الحوفضان) Qatil Ul Malook(قاتل الملوك)

144
00:11:02,303 --> 00:11:03,945
the one who would kill the kings.

145
00:11:04,238 --> 00:11:05,983
Does he belong to you.? They said: No

146
00:11:06,672 --> 00:11:09,472
He said: What about Al-Muzdaliff(مزدلف) Sahib Al-Imam Al-Mufradah(مفرده)

147
00:11:09,631 --> 00:11:12,007
Al-Muzdalaf(المزدلف), who had the unique turban.

148
00:11:12,285 --> 00:11:13,501
Does he belong to you.?

149
00:11:13,875 --> 00:11:14,605
They said: No

150
00:11:15,218 --> 00:11:20,217
He said: What about, are you the maternal uncle's of the Kings of Kinda(كنده).?

151
00:11:20,690 --> 00:11:21,475
They said: No

152
00:11:21,870 --> 00:11:25,165
Then are you the relatives of the kings of Lakham(لخم),

153
00:11:25,458 --> 00:11:26,446
They said: No

154
00:11:26,787 --> 00:11:28,377
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه said:

155
00:11:28,402 --> 00:11:30,750
Then you are not from the great Dahal(دهل), you are from the small Dahal(دهل).

156
00:11:31,590 --> 00:11:33,843
You don't belong to the great Dahal(دهل), you belong to the small Dahal(دهل).

157
00:11:35,262 --> 00:11:37,521
And look at the questions that he was asking,

158
00:11:37,810 --> 00:11:42,095
 it shows the detailed knowledge that Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه had.

159
00:11:44,117 --> 00:11:46,180
So, Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه was gonna leave

160
00:11:46,220 --> 00:11:50,757
but a young man they say, who just started to grow a beard he was very young in age.

161
00:11:51,365 --> 00:11:53,639
He came to Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) and he grabbed his camel

162
00:11:54,635 --> 00:11:57,526
and he said: You asked us and we responded.

163
00:11:57,792 --> 00:12:00,439
Now it's our turn to ask, and you respond.

164
00:12:01,353 --> 00:12:02,402
Where are you from.?

165
00:12:02,949 --> 00:12:05,719
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه said: I'm from Quraish(قريش).

166
00:12:06,535 --> 00:12:11,164
He said: Well then you are our leaders, I mean they all recognized Quraish(قريش).

167
00:12:12,098 --> 00:12:15,605
What part of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) are you from? He said: From Tame Bin Murah(تيم بن مرة).

168
00:12:16,070 --> 00:12:21,191
Tame(تيم) in Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) is seen as a very small and weak clan

169
00:12:21,649 --> 00:12:26,717
it's not among the larger ones, like Bannu Hashim(بنوهاشم), the family of Rasool Allah ﷺ

170
00:12:27,189 --> 00:12:30,987
or Bannu Makhzoom(بنومخزوم), the family of Khalid Bin Waleed(خالد بن وليد),

171
00:12:31,067 --> 00:12:34,426
these were the great families or Bannu Umayyah(بنوامية).

172
00:12:35,909 --> 00:12:41,488
So, Bannu Tame(بنوتيم) were very small in number and in the tribal society, your strength depends on your numbers.

173
00:12:41,544 --> 00:12:44,018
So, Tame(تيم) was a very small branch of Quraish(قريش).

174
00:12:44,380 --> 00:12:48,300
So, when this young man heard Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) say, I am from Tame(تيم)

175
00:12:48,532 --> 00:12:52,000
he said, you've shown the target shooter where to shoot.

176
00:12:52,604 --> 00:12:56,519
Meaning this is my opportunity to now ask you questions. He said:

177
00:12:57,243 --> 00:13:03,576
Does Qusae Bin Kulaab(قصئي بن كلاب), the one who defeated all of the invaders who wanted to invade Makkah

178
00:13:03,964 --> 00:13:09,668
and brought in Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) and unified them, and therefore he was called the unifier.

179
00:13:10,287 --> 00:13:12,194
 Is he from your people.?

180
00:13:12,597 --> 00:13:13,692
Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) said: No

181
00:13:14,377 --> 00:13:20,952
He said: What about Abd Manaaf(عبد المناف) who inherited everything from his father, is he from your people?

182
00:13:20,992 --> 00:13:21,612
He said: No

183
00:13:21,982 --> 00:13:24,303
What about Amr Bin Abd Manaf(عمرو بن عبد مناف)

184
00:13:24,458 --> 00:13:30,329
the one who used to crush bread in the soup for the pilgrims, and was called Hashem(هاشم).

185
00:13:30,932 --> 00:13:33,181
 Are you from his people? He said: No

186
00:13:33,412 --> 00:13:36,520
What about a Shaibat El-Hamd(شيبة الحمد), Abdul Muttalib(عبد المطلب).

187
00:13:36,821 --> 00:13:40,774
The one, who used to feed the animals in the land and the birds in the sea

188
00:13:41,075 --> 00:13:44,887
the man whom if you see his face is like the moon in the dark night.

189
00:13:45,477 --> 00:13:46,864
Are you from his family.?

190
00:13:47,178 --> 00:13:48,655
Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) said: No

191
00:13:48,892 --> 00:13:52,863
And then he asked him, then are you from the people of Ifadha(افاده) the ones, who take care of Al-Hajj(الحج).?

192
00:13:52,927 --> 00:13:53,617
He said: No!

193
00:13:53,846 --> 00:13:57,054
Are you the people of Hijaba(حجابه), the ones who have the key to Al-Ka'aba(الكعبه)

194
00:13:57,667 --> 00:13:58,467
He said: No

195
00:13:58,684 --> 00:14:03,683
Are you from the people of Nadwa(ندوه), the leadership of Quraish(قريش), the council?

196
00:14:03,767 --> 00:14:04,614
He said: No

197
00:14:04,814 --> 00:14:07,341
Are you from the people, who provide the pilgrims with water.

198
00:14:07,381 --> 00:14:07,900
He said: No

199
00:14:08,098 --> 00:14:10,034
Are you from the people, who feed the pilgrims.?

200
00:14:10,074 --> 00:14:10,725
He said: No

201
00:14:10,830 --> 00:14:14,504
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه was getting agitated with all of these questions

202
00:14:14,529 --> 00:14:16,006
that he has to say: No

203
00:14:16,409 --> 00:14:21,740
So, he pulled away his camel, and he walked, he just left the young man

204
00:14:22,244 --> 00:14:24,236
because it was becoming a bit embarrassing.

205
00:14:25,261 --> 00:14:27,987
So the young man smiled and he said:

206
00:14:28,124 --> 00:14:33,601
صادفه در السيلي درًا يدفع فتارةً يذهبه’ وتارةً يصدع

207
00:14:34,285 --> 00:14:36,311
It's a line poetry that he applied to this situation.

208
00:14:36,336 --> 00:14:39,646
He said: Your stream was overcome by my river

209
00:14:40,135 --> 00:14:42,829
that breaks it once and overrides it, another time.

210
00:14:43,911 --> 00:14:46,684
Meaning - You prove that we are from Dahal Al-Asghar(دهل الاصغر)

211
00:14:47,008 --> 00:14:50,291
and if you would have waited I would have showed you, where you belong to?

212
00:14:51,218 --> 00:14:54,462
Rasool Allah ﷺ, he saw this and he laughed.

213
00:14:55,779 --> 00:14:59,401
Ali Bin Abi Talib(علي بن ابي طالب) came to Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه and said:

214
00:14:59,520 --> 00:15:01,797
لقدوقع العرابي منك على باقية

215
00:15:02,075 --> 00:15:04,890
This Bedouin turned out to be a disaster for you.

216
00:15:05,855 --> 00:15:08,205
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه said: Yes

217
00:15:08,615 --> 00:15:12,953
For every problem there's a greater problem and our problems are caused by what we say.

218
00:15:13,512 --> 00:15:16,048
I'm the one who got myself into this trouble, in the first place.

219
00:15:17,693 --> 00:15:22,464
So then they moved on to another campground.

220
00:15:24,789 --> 00:15:27,627
Abu Bakr As-Siddiqueرضي الله عنه appointed to them and said:

221
00:15:29,006 --> 00:15:30,567
هَا أولآء غرورٌ الناس

222
00:15:30,639 --> 00:15:32,542
These are great people.

223
00:15:34,899 --> 00:15:36,213
So let's go to them.

224
00:15:37,946 --> 00:15:40,497
So, they went there and these were from Bannu Shaibaan(بنوشعيبان)

225
00:15:40,583 --> 00:15:42,516
Bannu Shaibaan(بنوشعيبان) are also tribe from Iraq.

226
00:15:42,849 --> 00:15:45,284
And by the way, Imam Ahmad Bin Hanbal(امام احمد بن حنبل) is from Bannu Shaibaan(بنوشعيبان)

227
00:15:45,457 --> 00:15:47,025
Imam Ahmad Bin Hanbal Shaibani(امام احمد بن حنبل ألشعيباني).

228
00:15:49,101 --> 00:15:51,005
So they went to Bannu Shaibaan(بنوشعيبان)

229
00:15:51,360 --> 00:15:54,770
and their leaders were there, Mafrooq(مفروق) and Hani Bin Qubaisa(هاني بن قبيسه)

230
00:15:54,993 --> 00:15:58,499
and An-Nouman Bin Shuraik(النعمان بن شريق) and Musanna Bin Harissa Shaibani(مثنى بن حارثه شعيباني),

231
00:15:58,753 --> 00:16:02,439
who later became one of the great generals in the Muslim armies.

232
00:16:03,074 --> 00:16:06,960
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه again notice that Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) is the one who's doing the speaking

233
00:16:07,110 --> 00:16:09,525
not Muhammadﷺ, he was his spokesman.

234
00:16:10,929 --> 00:16:13,169
He was the spokesperson of Muhammadﷺ.

235
00:16:13,747 --> 00:16:15,525
So, Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) walked up to them

236
00:16:16,185 --> 00:16:20,815
and then he asked Mafrooq(مفروق), who was the closest one to him.

237
00:16:21,296 --> 00:16:25,997
He asked him, How large is your fighting force?

238
00:16:27,426 --> 00:16:28,640
He said: One Thousand

239
00:16:30,077 --> 00:16:34,124
Which was a large number in the desert. He said:

240
00:16:34,181 --> 00:16:35,483
وكيف المنع فيكم

241
00:16:35,816 --> 00:16:37,481
And how good is your protection?

242
00:16:38,082 --> 00:16:40,179
He said: We do our best.

243
00:16:41,661 --> 00:16:47,428
He then asked him, and what are the results of your wars against your enemies?

244
00:16:48,813 --> 00:16:51,198
He said, or actually, before that he asked him,

245
00:16:51,627 --> 00:16:53,834
he said: How strong are you in war?

246
00:16:54,347 --> 00:16:59,347
Mafrooq(مفروق) responded by saying, we prefer our horses over our children

247
00:16:59,653 --> 00:17:02,377
and we prefer our weapons over our camels.

248
00:17:03,397 --> 00:17:07,694
He said: So, what are the results of your wars with your enemies?

249
00:17:07,980 --> 00:17:10,915
He said: It is Allah, Who gives victory.

250
00:17:11,260 --> 00:17:14,096
One day we win, one day we lose.

251
00:17:17,407 --> 00:17:24,196
Because of these questions this man thought that the one was asking might be Muhammadﷺ.

252
00:17:24,735 --> 00:17:28,210
Because they heard about Muhammadﷺ and they knew that he's looking for protection

253
00:17:29,058 --> 00:17:31,719
and that's where all of these questions were leading to.

254
00:17:32,012 --> 00:17:32,539
So he said:

255
00:17:32,579 --> 00:17:33,683
لعلك اخى قريش

256
00:17:34,054 --> 00:17:35,569
Are you the man from Quraish(قُرَيْشْ)?

257
00:17:35,745 --> 00:17:37,426
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه said;

258
00:17:37,724 --> 00:17:41,601
If you are referring to the Messenger of Allah, Muhammadﷺ, This is him.

259
00:17:42,735 --> 00:17:45,161
And he pointed to Muhammadﷺ.

260
00:17:45,478 --> 00:17:47,159
Mafrooq(مفروق) responded by saying;

261
00:17:47,351 --> 00:17:50,014
We heard that he claims to be the Messenger of Allah.

262
00:17:51,124 --> 00:17:54,122
So, the news of Muhammadﷺ even though, they didn't see him yet

263
00:17:54,211 --> 00:17:57,812
the news of Muhammadﷺ has spread all the way to Iraq.

264
00:18:00,957 --> 00:18:05,738
So, Mafrooq(مفروق) now, turned to Muhammad صلوات الله وسلام عليه and said;

265
00:18:05,906 --> 00:18:06,933
إلى ماذا تدعو

266
00:18:07,539 --> 00:18:08,732
What is your message?

267
00:18:10,030 --> 00:18:16,805
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: My message is to call to Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ, that there is no one worthy of worship, but Him.

268
00:18:17,254 --> 00:18:20,646
And that I am the messenger of Allah, صلى الله عليه وسلم.

269
00:18:21,299 --> 00:18:25,812
And, and he went on reciting some Ayaat(آيات), from Surat Al-An'aam(سورة الانعام)

270
00:18:26,917 --> 00:18:28,688
that talk about the virtues of Islam

271
00:18:28,712 --> 00:18:31,330
and some things that were Halal(حلال) and some things that were Haram(حرام).

272
00:18:32,286 --> 00:18:35,880
They were very impressed with the Ayaat(آيات) of Qur'an, so they wanted to hear more.

273
00:18:36,041 --> 00:18:39,178
He said: Tell me more. So, Rasool Allah ﷺ said:

274
00:18:39,202 --> 00:18:42,308
إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ يَأْمُرُ بِٱلْعَدْلِ وَٱلْإِحْسَٰنِ وَإِيتَائِ ذِى ٱلْقُرْبَىٰ

275
00:18:42,475 --> 00:18:46,707
وَيَنْهَىٰ عَنِ ٱلْفَحْشَاءِ وَٱلْمُنكَرِ وَٱلْبَغْىِ ۚ يَعِظُكُمْ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَذَكَّرُونَ

276
00:18:48,579 --> 00:18:52,925
Mafrooq(مفروق) said: What you have called to, is a very noble message

277
00:18:53,757 --> 00:19:01,030
and the people, who have treated you in an evil way are truly evil people.

278
00:19:01,906 --> 00:19:06,215
If this is your message, then the people, who are against you, are evil people.

279
00:19:07,439 --> 00:19:11,373
He recognize that from the beauty of the Ayaat(آيات) of Qur'an and the virtues of Islam.

280
00:19:13,885 --> 00:19:19,413
But then Mafrooq(مفروق) didn't want to take the decision and become a Muslim because he has to consult.

281
00:19:19,878 --> 00:19:25,090
So he said: And here is our religious leader Haani Bin Qubaisah(هاني بن قبيسه)

282
00:19:25,556 --> 00:19:26,874
why don't you get his opinion?

283
00:19:27,330 --> 00:19:30,312
So he pointed towards Hannah(هانه), and said to Rasool Allah ﷺ

284
00:19:30,336 --> 00:19:31,485
why didn't you get his opinion?

285
00:19:32,612 --> 00:19:38,339
Haani Bin Qubaisah(هاني بن قبيسه) said: Yes! What you are calling to, is a noble message.

286
00:19:38,985 --> 00:19:45,700
However, it is not appropriate for us to accept this religion and join it

287
00:19:46,017 --> 00:19:48,489
 just because of one meeting that we had with you

288
00:19:49,696 --> 00:19:53,522
that is hastening, and that is unwise,

289
00:19:53,974 --> 00:19:58,907
but we have to go back consult our people, and we will wait, and you wait.

290
00:20:00,990 --> 00:20:04,112
So, he have nothing wrong to say about Islam, but he said:

291
00:20:04,475 --> 00:20:07,634
It's not appropriate for us, just make a decision right here on the spot.

292
00:20:07,865 --> 00:20:10,168
We have to think about it, we have to consult our people,

293
00:20:10,509 --> 00:20:13,108
because we have left some of our leaders, back home.

294
00:20:14,628 --> 00:20:20,087
And then he turned on the attention to Al-Muthana Bin Harissa(المثني بن حارثه).

295
00:20:20,841 --> 00:20:22,963
And he said and here is Al-Muthana Bin Harissa(المثني بن حارثه)

296
00:20:23,218 --> 00:20:24,997
why don't you hear what he has to say?

297
00:20:25,616 --> 00:20:30,433
So, Al-Muthanna Bin Harissa(المثني بن حارثه) said: I agree with what Hannah(هانه) said,

298
00:20:30,812 --> 00:20:32,832
that your message is a noble message.

299
00:20:34,532 --> 00:20:37,187
But we are people who are between two wings

300
00:20:37,793 --> 00:20:39,369
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: What is that?

301
00:20:39,927 --> 00:20:44,795
He said: On one side it is Persia, and on one side is the land of the Arabs.

302
00:20:45,775 --> 00:20:48,974
Bannu Sahibaan(بنوشعيبان) were on the borders of the Persian Empire.

303
00:20:51,392 --> 00:20:53,069
Al-Muthanna Bin Harissa(المثني بن حارثه) said;

304
00:20:54,776 --> 00:21:03,363
Our agreement with the Persians, is that we do not give refuge to anybody who has committed a crime.

305
00:21:04,251 --> 00:21:08,914
And I think that what you are calling to, is something that kings do not like.

306
00:21:09,435 --> 00:21:13,720
Subhaan Allah(سبحان الله) look at the wisdom, and this was just out of one meeting.

307
00:21:14,286 --> 00:21:19,418
He said: I think that what you are calling to, this religion is not something that kings like.

308
00:21:20,415 --> 00:21:24,573
Therefore, we can promise you protection from the side of the Arabs

309
00:21:24,851 --> 00:21:27,770
but we cannot promise you protection from the side of the Persians,

310
00:21:28,985 --> 00:21:33,729
because they do not forgive, this is an empire.

311
00:21:34,745 --> 00:21:37,397
They will be very unforgiving but with the Arabs you can give and take.

312
00:21:38,157 --> 00:21:42,615
Tribes, just like us, but with the Persians, we cannot promise you protection.

313
00:21:43,771 --> 00:21:46,588
So, it was half a deal, it was better than nothing.

314
00:21:46,975 --> 00:21:50,408
Rasool Allah ﷺ in Makkah had nothing, it was a dead end.

315
00:21:51,085 --> 00:21:54,933
Atleast they are willing to give Rasool Allah ﷺ opportunity to make Da'wah(دعوة)

316
00:21:55,148 --> 00:21:57,317
towards one side, but not to the other.

317
00:21:58,243 --> 00:22:01,350
But did Rasool Allah ﷺ takes the offer, or did he refuse it?

318
00:22:02,076 --> 00:22:03,621
Rasool Allah ﷺ said:

319
00:22:04,079 --> 00:22:05,248
ما أسئل تم الرد

320
00:22:05,658 --> 00:22:09,200
Your response was very nice, very polite

321
00:22:10,060 --> 00:22:14,633
ولكن الهذالأمرلا يقوم إلَّا لِمن أحاطه من كُلِّ جوانب

322
00:22:15,125 --> 00:22:20,862
But this is a religion that cannot stand, unless it is surrounded from every direction.

323
00:22:21,516 --> 00:22:26,754
This is a religion that cannot stand unless you offer it protection from every side.

324
00:22:28,188 --> 00:22:31,522
This issue needs to be protected from every direction.

325
00:22:31,878 --> 00:22:35,139
You cannot offer me protection from one side, and not from the other.

326
00:22:35,163 --> 00:22:36,467
ادْخُلُوا فِي السِّلْمِ كَافَّةً

327
00:22:36,721 --> 00:22:41,199
With Islam, you don't give and take, you don't pick and choose, you take it all.

328
00:22:42,305 --> 00:22:45,740
اللہ عز و جل أغنى الشركاء عن الشرك

329
00:22:46,440 --> 00:22:50,500
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ, does not want any partner with Him.

330
00:22:51,117 --> 00:22:54,351
Therefore if you give something to Allah and you give something to someone else.

331
00:22:54,376 --> 00:22:56,534
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ refuses that,

332
00:22:56,964 --> 00:22:59,886
because Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ wants you to give everything to Him

333
00:23:00,608 --> 00:23:06,202
all of your heart goes to Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ, the Muhabbah(محبه) of Allah سبحانه وتعالى.

334
00:23:07,335 --> 00:23:10,293
Therefore, we cannot sacrifice partially

335
00:23:10,318 --> 00:23:13,327
but we have to sacrifice everything for the sake of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ.

336
00:23:14,708 --> 00:23:16,733
Anyway, that was the end of the conversation,

337
00:23:17,190 --> 00:23:19,641
so Rasool Allah ﷺ left.

338
00:23:19,906 --> 00:23:21,370
Ali Bin Abi Talib(علي بن ابي طالب) says;

339
00:23:21,872 --> 00:23:28,131
ولقد رأيت رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم سرَّ بما كان من أمري أبي بكر ومعارفته با الناس

340
00:23:28,448 --> 00:23:36,106
And I've seen that Rasool Allah ﷺ was extremely pleased with the conduct of Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه,

341
00:23:36,312 --> 00:23:37,563
and his knowledge about people.

342
00:23:38,346 --> 00:23:39,675
Rasool Allah ﷺ was very happy.

343
00:23:42,218 --> 00:23:47,907
I gave you the talk about this conversation, just to show you some of the abilities of Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه

344
00:23:47,946 --> 00:23:50,947
that were bestowed by Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ.

345
00:23:52,261 --> 00:23:59,678
The next part of our journey is very critical event in the life of Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه

346
00:24:00,011 --> 00:24:04,814
and it's also a very critical event in the entire life of the Ummah(أمة),

347
00:24:05,209 --> 00:24:06,795
and that is the Hijrah An-Nabwiyah(هجرة النبويه).

348
00:24:07,666 --> 00:24:10,422
Ayesha رضي الله عنها says and this is in Al-Bukhari(البخاري),

349
00:24:10,974 --> 00:24:13,997
that one day during the heat of noon.

350
00:24:14,909 --> 00:24:19,224
We saw Rasool Allah ﷺ coming to us and he was veiled, he was masked

351
00:24:20,431 --> 00:24:24,548
he had a turban wrapped around his face.

352
00:24:26,292 --> 00:24:32,601
Now Ayesha رضي الله عنها says that Rasool Allah ﷺ would visit us every day once or twice on a daily basis,

353
00:24:32,935 --> 00:24:35,911
 but that particular visit was unusual because it was at noon

354
00:24:36,274 --> 00:24:42,530
and at noon in Arabia, because of the heat, people usually take a break, a nap.

355
00:24:43,278 --> 00:24:49,513
Business stops until the climate calms down, and then they go out again.

356
00:24:50,314 --> 00:24:53,060
So, that was a time when there was no one, on the streets of Makkah.

357
00:24:53,603 --> 00:24:57,429
That is when Rasool Allah ﷺ made his visit to Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه so he came in.

358
00:24:58,460 --> 00:24:59,964
 Ayesha رضي الله عنها says:

359
00:25:00,262 --> 00:25:01,598
Abu Bakr As-Siddique(ابو بكر الصديق) said:

360
00:25:01,952 --> 00:25:06,293
Rasool Allah ﷺ would not come in this time, unless there's something important going on

361
00:25:06,697 --> 00:25:07,406
أمرٌ جلاً

362
00:25:07,895 --> 00:25:08,966
There's something serious.

363
00:25:09,538 --> 00:25:11,744
So, he went to meet Rasool Allah ﷺ, Rasool Ullah said:

364
00:25:11,958 --> 00:25:13,032
أخرج ما عندك

365
00:25:13,374 --> 00:25:14,730
Empty your house.

366
00:25:15,443 --> 00:25:19,734
Rasool Allah ﷺ had the secret and he wanted the house to be empty.

367
00:25:20,877 --> 00:25:22,496
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه said:

368
00:25:22,574 --> 00:25:23,980
إنَّما هم أهلك

369
00:25:24,242 --> 00:25:25,891
This is your family

370
00:25:28,542 --> 00:25:31,359
everyone in my house is your family,

371
00:25:32,262 --> 00:25:37,338
consider them to be your family, so your secret is their secret.

372
00:25:39,309 --> 00:25:43,940
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: I have been given permission to make Hijrah(هجرة).

373
00:25:45,617 --> 00:25:47,775
Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) the first thing he said was

