747
00:53:02,062 --> 00:53:07,644
So Ibraheem عليه السّلام said, and who will hear me my voice will not reach to the people, there's no one around.

748
00:53:07,997 --> 00:53:11,927
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ told him, you make the call, and I will convey the message

749
00:53:13,002 --> 00:53:15,132
you just make the call and I will convey the message.

750
00:53:15,675 --> 00:53:20,419
Well the message was conveyed the invitation of Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) was given to us through Qur'an.

751
00:53:21,249 --> 00:53:27,498
So the words of Ibraheem عليه السّلام have reached millions and millions of people actually billions.

752
00:53:29,286 --> 00:53:32,024
All what Ibraheem(ابراهيم) had to do, is make the call عليه السلام.

753
00:53:32,320 --> 00:53:34,316
And Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ conveyed it to us.

754
00:53:35,024 --> 00:53:38,988
So, they loved Makkah and for the Muhajireen(مهاجرين) this was extremely difficult to leave Makkah.

755
00:53:39,140 --> 00:53:43,469
In addition to that, Al-Madina wasn't a very pleasant place.

756
00:53:44,926 --> 00:53:48,563
It was described as having a lot of stagnant water

757
00:53:49,216 --> 00:53:51,893
when floods would come, they would stagnate,

758
00:53:52,206 --> 00:53:57,392
and the water would become very smelly and it was very epidemic.

759
00:53:57,926 --> 00:54:04,027
 A lot of disease breakouts in Al-Madina an endemic environment.

760
00:54:05,012 --> 00:54:07,645
Now the people of Madina grew up in there, so they were used to it

761
00:54:07,685 --> 00:54:11,111
 and their bodies developed resistance to those diseases.

762
00:54:11,228 --> 00:54:14,283
But with Al-Muhajireen(المهاجرين), when they came in, they fell sick

763
00:54:14,865 --> 00:54:17,849
and they got this very severe fever

764
00:54:20,384 --> 00:54:23,191
modern scholars say that it might have been malaria

765
00:54:23,382 --> 00:54:28,869
because of the existence of stagnant water and all of that it could have been malaria breakouts but Allah ho Alam(الله اعلم).

766
00:54:29,035 --> 00:54:33,507
It was described in our books of Seerah(سيرة), in history as fever breakouts.

767
00:54:34,781 --> 00:54:38,714
I just want you to imagine, with Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) or any one of the Sahabah(صحابه)

768
00:54:39,987 --> 00:54:48,105
feeling homesick alright and what a painful feeling that is homesick to Makkah.

769
00:54:49,497 --> 00:54:51,149
You're separated from your families

770
00:54:53,824 --> 00:54:59,381
and then you become sick and ill, and if there's no one to care for you from your family,

771
00:55:00,358 --> 00:55:05,585
and you're not staying in your house, you've left your bed, and you're a foreigner.

772
00:55:06,541 --> 00:55:08,533
Can you imagine how difficult those feelings are?

773
00:55:09,952 --> 00:55:15,756
Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) was living with Bilal(بلال) and Aamir Bin Fuhairah(عامر بن فهيره) his servant.

774
00:55:16,232 --> 00:55:17,495
They were sharing the same room.

775
00:55:18,385 --> 00:55:21,960
Rasool Allah ﷺ told Ayesha(عائشه), O Ayesha(عائشه) go and take care of them.

776
00:55:23,761 --> 00:55:27,197
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ has blessed Muhammadﷺ, he didn't get affected with that fever.

777
00:55:27,967 --> 00:55:29,742
But the other Muhajireen(مهاجرين) and they were going through it.

778
00:55:30,411 --> 00:55:32,669
So Rasool Allah ﷺ told Ayesha(عائشه) go and take care of them.

779
00:55:34,863 --> 00:55:37,152
He felt for his Sahabah(الصحابه) and he cared about them a lot.

780
00:55:37,952 --> 00:55:42,170
So Ayesha رضي الله عنها says, I went there and this was before Al-Hijab(حجاب).

781
00:55:42,697 --> 00:55:48,563
So I went there and I walked up to my father and I said;

782
00:55:48,823 --> 00:55:50,702
يا ابتي كيف تجدك؟

783
00:55:50,857 --> 00:55:52,437
O my father, How are you doing.?

784
00:55:53,516 --> 00:55:57,364
So, my father responded by a line of poetry and he said:

785
00:55:57,821 --> 00:56:02,115
كُلٌ مرِعٍ أصبحٌ في أهله والموت أدْنى مِشراكٍ أليه

786
00:56:03,556 --> 00:56:14,517
He said, Every one of us is spending their day while death could be closer to them than the strap on their shoes,

787
00:56:15,896 --> 00:56:22,039
the strap of their shoes means it's very close to you he was talking about death.

788
00:56:22,350 --> 00:56:25,352
Ayesha رضي الله عنها said: My father doesn't know, what he's saying.

789
00:56:25,834 --> 00:56:30,127
The fever was so bad it was causing hallucinations.

790
00:56:32,024 --> 00:56:34,404
You can imagine how severe the fever was.

791
00:56:34,817 --> 00:56:35,516
She said;

792
00:56:35,536 --> 00:56:36,564
أبي لا يعقل ما يبقي

793
00:56:36,624 --> 00:56:38,010
My father doesn't know what he's saying.

794
00:56:38,497 --> 00:56:41,035
And then she went to Aamir Bin Fuhairah(عامر بن فهيره) and she said:

795
00:56:41,059 --> 00:56:42,185
Aamir(عامر)! How are you.?

796
00:56:43,614 --> 00:56:45,104
So he responded by saying,

797
00:56:45,658 --> 00:56:49,599
لقد وجدت الموت  قبل زوقيه إنَّ جبعنا حتْفهو من فوقه

798
00:56:50,189 --> 00:56:55,079
I've seen death before I could taste it and even the coward will eventually die.

799
00:56:56,244 --> 00:56:58,623
She said, and Aamir(عامر) doesn't know, what he's saying.

800
00:57:00,800 --> 00:57:03,790
And then she said: She went to Bilal(بلال) and she asked him, how were you doing

801
00:57:03,821 --> 00:57:07,739
and she said he was unconscious and whenever he would regain consciousness,

802
00:57:07,836 --> 00:57:09,670
 he would sit up in the middle of the room

803
00:57:09,732 --> 00:57:12,608
he would sit in the middle of the room, and speak to himself

804
00:57:12,633 --> 00:57:14,654
and he would raise his voice by saying:

805
00:57:15,134 --> 00:57:17,499
ألا ليلة شهري هل أبيتنَّ ليلةً

806
00:57:17,852 --> 00:57:20,312
بوادٍ وحولي إزخَرًا وجليلُ

807
00:57:20,551 --> 00:57:25,146
وهل أردنا يومًا مياحه مجنةٍ وهل يبدوانَّ لي شامةٌ وطفيلُ

808
00:57:25,873 --> 00:57:31,138
He said: We'll I ever spend a night in a valley surrounded by Izkhar(ازخر) and Jalil(جليل).

809
00:57:31,384 --> 00:57:33,672
Izkhar(ازخر) and Jalil(جليل) are two plants that grow in Makkah.

810
00:57:34,226 --> 00:57:37,471
He said: Will there ever come a time, when I would spend my night

811
00:57:37,600 --> 00:57:40,649
in a valley surrounded by Izkhar(ازخر) and Jalil(جليل)

812
00:57:41,074 --> 00:57:43,637
and will I ever visit the waters of Majannah(مجنة) in Makkah

813
00:57:43,946 --> 00:57:48,195
and will I ever see Shaama(شامه) and Tafeel(طفيل), two mountains in Makkah

814
00:57:48,632 --> 00:57:50,904
feeling homesick to Makkah - Bilal رضي الله عنه.

815
00:57:51,265 --> 00:57:53,556
And he's raising his voice with these lines of poetry

816
00:57:54,946 --> 00:57:58,327
Ayesha رضي الله عنها, she went back to Muhammadﷺ

817
00:57:58,692 --> 00:58:02,421
and told him what was happening, Rasool Allah ﷺ cried.

818
00:58:03,927 --> 00:58:05,775
Because Rasool Allah ﷺ was the one, who brought them here.

819
00:58:07,270 --> 00:58:11,938
They sacrificed their homes, they sacrifice their families.

820
00:58:12,444 --> 00:58:20,907
They left Makkah and they came to a foreign land suffered from diseases, they did that for Muhammadﷺ.

821
00:58:21,892 --> 00:58:25,113
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ cried. And then he made the Dua(دعا)

822
00:58:26,100 --> 00:58:31,392
اللهم حبب إلينا المدينةَ كحبنا مكة أو أشدَّ حبَّا،

823
00:58:32,265 --> 00:58:36,520
 أللهم باركلنا في مدِّها وسعيها وأنقل هُمَّاحا إلى جهفة

824
00:58:37,234 --> 00:58:40,476
In Bukhari(بخاري) Rasool Allah ﷺ made this Dua(دعا) and said;

825
00:58:40,500 --> 00:58:45,554
O Allah make us love Madina, like we love Makkah or more.

826
00:58:46,652 --> 00:58:51,287
And O Allah make it's blessed and O Allah take the fever of it,

827
00:58:51,526 --> 00:58:53,726
out of the Madina and put it in Al-Juhffah(جهفه).

828
00:58:56,621 --> 00:58:58,224
How did Makkah become blessed?

829
00:58:59,135 --> 00:59:01,697
Through the Dua(دعا) of Ibraheem عليه السّلام.

830
00:59:02,835 --> 00:59:06,015
Al-Madina at that moment had nothing special to it

831
00:59:06,528 --> 00:59:10,216
but Rasool Allah ﷺ made this Dua(دعا) to bless Madina

832
00:59:11,057 --> 00:59:15,140
and Rasool Allah ﷺ made the Dua(دعا) to make it more beloved to us than Makkah.

833
00:59:15,996 --> 00:59:22,667
And since then every believer loves Madina more than Makkah.

834
00:59:24,225 --> 00:59:29,105
If you visited Makkah and Madina when you get inside Madina you have this completely different feeling,

835
00:59:30,048 --> 00:59:31,332
 tranquility is in the air.

836
00:59:32,448 --> 00:59:35,541
It is the Barakah(بركة) of the Dua(دعا) of Rasool Allah ﷺ,

837
00:59:36,302 --> 00:59:40,364
اللهم حبب إلينا المدينةَ كحبنا مكة أو أشدَّ حبَّا،

838
00:59:41,042 --> 00:59:44,882
And it's in fact the sign of Eeman(ايمان) to love Al-Madina.

839
00:59:47,203 --> 00:59:54,142
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه and the Sahabah(صحابه) who were crying and longing to go back to Makkah

840
00:59:56,103 --> 00:59:59,340
never went back even when they had the chance to do so.

841
01:00:00,091 --> 01:00:04,689
And when Makkah was opened they all went back with Rasool Allah ﷺ to Al-Madina

842
01:00:05,336 --> 01:00:07,556
and Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) chose it to be, his capital

843
01:00:07,964 --> 01:00:11,506
and so did Umar Ibn Khattab(عمر إبن خطاب) and so did Uthman رضي الله عنهم.

844
01:00:11,707 --> 01:00:14,958
And if it wasn't for the circumstances that forced Ali(علي) out

845
01:00:15,418 --> 01:00:19,472
he would have remained in there too, رضي الله عنه ، رضي الله عن صحابه اجمعين.

846
01:00:21,074 --> 01:00:26,745
وصلوات الله ولسلام علي سيد الأولين والآخرين والحمدلله رب العلمين

